<report>
<title>Sample size for survival analysis</title>
<line></line>
<line>median survival time for controls = <inu>ctFmt</inu></line>
<line>hazard ratio = <inu>hrFmt</inu></line>
<line>accrual time for recruitment = <inu>atFmt</inu></line>
<line>additional follow-up time after recruitment = <inu>futFmt</inu></line>
<line>alpha = <inu>alpha</inu></line>
<line>power = <inu>power</inu></line>
<line></line>
<line>Estimated minimum sample size = <in>size</in> experimental subjects and <in>controls</in> controls</line>
<block name="assumptions">
<line></line>
<line><warn>NB:Assumptions of this calculation may cause over estimation of sample size when power is low.  However, true power associated with <in>cases</in> cases will be no less than <in>no_less</in> and no greater than <in>no_greater</in>.</warn></line>
</block>
</report>
